==Pre-match==
===Ambassador===
[[File:Éric_Abidal_-_001.jpg|thumb|upright|[[Eric Abidal]] was named as the ambassador for the final.]]
The ambassador for the final was former French international [[Eric Abidal]], who played three seasons at [[Olympique Lyonnais|Lyon]] and later won two UEFA Champions League titles with [[FC Barcelona|Barcelona]].

===Ticketing===
With a stadium capacity of 57,000 for the final, a total amount of 23,000 tickets were available to fans and the general public, with the two finalist teams receiving tickets (number to be confirmed) each and with the other tickets being available for sale to fans worldwide via UEFA.com from 15 to 22 March 2018 in four price categories: €150, €100, €70, and €45. The remaining tickets were allocated to the local organising committee, UEFA and national associations, commercial partners and broadcasters, and to serve the corporate hospitality programme.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.uefa.com/uefaeuropaleague/news/0244-0e98adc14742-ebd3fa3ee04d-1000--europa-league-final-ticket-resale-window-closed/ |title=UEFA Europa League final ticket application window |work=UEFA.com |publisher=Union of European Football Associations |date=12 March 2018}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.uefa.com/insideuefa/mediaservices/newsid=2544812.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180315152021/http://www.uefa.com/insideuefa/mediaservices/newsid=2544812.html|url-status=dead|archive-date=15 March 2018|title=General public tickets for 2018 UEFA Europa League final in Lyon go on sale|publisher=[[UEFA]]|date=15 March 2018}}</ref>

===Officials===
On 7 May 2018, UEFA announced that Dutchman [[Björn Kuipers]] would officiate the final. It was the second time he was appointed for a [[UEFA Europa League]] final, as he had already been the referee in the [[2013 UEFA Europa League Final|2013 final]]. He was also the referee for the [[2014 UEFA Champions League Final]], which Atlético lost to [[Real Madrid CF|Real Madrid]] in [[Overtime (sports)#Association football|extra time]]. He was joined by his fellow countrymen, with Sander van Roekel and Erwin Zeinstra as assistant referees, [[Danny Makkelie]] and [[Pol van Boekel]] as additional assistant referees, and Mario Diks as reserve assistant referee. The fourth official for the final was [[Szymon Marciniak]] from Poland.<ref name="officials">{{cite news |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefaeuropaleague/news/0245-0e98c4c96761-9c30cce04a5b-1000--bjorn-kuipers-to-referee-europa-league-final/ |title=Björn Kuipers to referee Europa League final |work=UEFA.com |publisher=Union of European Football Associations |date=7 May 2018 |access-date=7 May 2018}}</ref>

===Opening ceremony===
French DJ duo [[Ofenbach (DJs)|Ofenbach]] performed at the opening ceremony preceding the final.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefaeuropaleague/news/0244-0e98aacb9053-7d6eb559b048-1000--ofenbach-to-perform-at-uefa-europa-league-final/ |title=Ofenbach to perform at UEFA Europa League final |work=UEFA.com |publisher=Union of European Football Associations |date=13 April 2018 |access-date=16 May 2018}}</ref>

==Match==

===Summary===
In the 21st minute, [[André-Frank Zambo Anguissa]] miss-controlled a pass out from goalkeeper [[Steve Mandanda]], the ball came to [[Gabi (footballer, born 1983)|Gabi]] who passed into [[Antoine Griezmann]] who scored with a low shot into the bottom left corner. Marseille captain [[Dimitri Payet]] left the match due to injury in the 32nd minute. It was 2–0 in the 49th minute when Antoine Griezmann dinked the ball past the advancing Steve Mandanda and into the bottom left from inside the penalty area after a pass from [[Koke (footballer, born 1992)|Koke]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/44113764|title =Marseille 0 Atletico Madrid 3|date=16 May 2018|work=BBC Sport|access-date=23 May 2018}}</ref> Gabi got the third goal in the 89th minute with a low right foot finish from the right after another pass from Koke.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/live/2018/may/16/marseille-v-atletico-madrid-europa-league-final-live|title =Marseille 0 Atletico Madrid 3: As it happened|date=16 May 2018|work=Guardian|access-date=23 May 2018}}</ref>

===Details===
The "home" team (for administrative purposes) was determined by an additional draw held after the semi-final draw, which was held on 13 April 2018, 12:00 [[Central European Summer Time|CEST]], at the UEFA headquarters in [[Nyon]], Switzerland.<ref name="drawSF">{{cite web|url=https://www.uefa.com/uefaeuropaleague/draws/2018/2000894/|title=Semi-final and final draws|publisher=[[UEFA]]}}</ref>

